---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import { SITE_TITLE, SITE_URL } from '../consts';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead
			title={`Privacy Policy - ${SITE_TITLE}`}
			description={`Privacy Policy, Cookie Disclosure, and Advertising standards (Google AdSense) for ${SITE_TITLE}.`}
		/>
	</head>
	<body class="bg-[#0b0f19] min-h-screen flex flex-col text-slate-200">
		<Header />

		<main class="grow max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 py-12">
			<!-- Header Section -->
			<div class="mb-10 text-center">
				<span class="inline-block px-3 py-1 text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-amber-400 bg-amber-950/60 border border-amber-800/50 rounded-md mb-3">
					TRANSPARENCY & DATA PRIVACY
				</span>
				<h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-extrabold text-white tracking-tight">
					Privacy Policy
				</h1>
				<p class="mt-3 text-xs text-slate-400">
					Last Updated: November 24, 2026 &bull; Effective Immediately
				</p>
			</div>

			<!-- Main Content Document -->
			<div class="bg-[#111827] rounded-2xl shadow-xl border border-slate-800 p-6 sm:p-10 space-y-8 text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
				<div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-amber-950/20 border border-amber-800/40 text-xs text-amber-200 leading-relaxed">
					<strong>Commitment to Reader Privacy:</strong> At <strong>{SITE_TITLE}</strong> (accessible at {SITE_URL}), the privacy of our visitors is one of our primary priorities. This Privacy Policy document outlines the types of information collected and recorded by {SITE_TITLE} and how we use it in accordance with standard web practices and Google Publisher Policies.
				</div>

				<section>
					<h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-3 pb-2 border-b border-slate-800">
						1. Log Files
					</h2>
					<p>
						<strong>{SITE_TITLE}</strong> follows a standard procedure of using log files. The information collected by log files includes internet protocol (IP) addresses, browser type, Internet Service Provider (ISP), date and time stamp, referring/exit pages, and possibly the number of clicks. These are not linked to any information that is personally identifiable.
					</p>
				</section>

				<section>
					<h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-3 pb-2 border-b border-slate-800">
						2. Cookies and Web Beacons
					</h2>
					<p>
						Like any other website, <strong>{SITE_TITLE}</strong> uses "cookies". These cookies are used to store information including visitors' preferences, and the pages on the website that the visitor accessed or visited. The information is used to optimize the users' experience by customizing our web page content based on visitors' browser type and/or other information.
					</p>
				</section>

				<section class="p-6 bg-[#070a12] rounded-xl border border-slate-800">
					<h2 class="text-lg sm:text-xl font-bold text-white mb-3 pb-2 border-b border-slate-800 flex items-center gap-2">
						<span class="text-amber-400">3.</span> Google DoubleClick DART Cookie & Advertising
					</h2>
					<p class="text-sm">
						Google is one of a third-party vendor on our site. It also uses cookies, known as DART cookies, to serve ads to our site visitors based upon their visit to our website and other sites on the internet.
					</p>
					<ul class="list-disc pl-6 mt-3 space-y-2 text-sm text-slate-400">
						<li>
							Third-party vendors, including Google, use cookies to serve ads based on a user's prior visits to your website or other websites.
						</li>
						<li>
							Google's use of advertising cookies enables it and its partners to serve ads to your users based on their visit to your sites and/or other sites on the Internet.
						</li>
						<li>
							Visitors may opt out of personalized advertising by visiting Ads Settings or by visiting <a href="https://www.aboutads.info" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-amber-400 underline font-semibold">www.aboutads.info</a>.
						</li>
					</ul>
				</section>

				<section>
					<h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-3 pb-2 border-b border-slate-800">
						4. California Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA) Rights
					</h2>
					<p>
						Under the CCPA, California consumers have the right to request disclosure of categories and specific pieces of personal data collected, request deletion of personal data, and request that a business not sell their personal data.
					</p>
				</section>

				<section>
					<h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-3 pb-2 border-b border-slate-800">
						5. Children's Privacy Protection (COPPA)
					</h2>
					<p>
						<strong>{SITE_TITLE}</strong> does not knowingly collect any Personal Identifiable Information from children under the age of 13. If you think that your child provided this kind of information on our website, we strongly encourage you to contact us immediately.
					</p>
				</section>

				<section>
					<h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-3 pb-2 border-b border-slate-800">
						6. Your Consent
					</h2>
					<p>
						By using our website, you hereby consent to our Privacy Policy and agree to its Terms and Conditions.
					</p>
				</section>
			</div>
		</main>

		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>
